$\begin{align*}\underset{\sim}{v}(t)&=(2t-8)\underset{\sim}{i}+(3t^2-75)\underset{\sim}{j}\\\dot{x}=0:\quad 2t-8&=0\\t&=4\\\dot{y}=0:\quad 3t^2-75&=0\\t^2&=25\\t&=5\end{align*}$
Reject $t=-5$ because $t\ge0$. The components never vanish together, so the particle is never at rest.
At $t=4$, $\underset{\sim}{v}(4)=-27\underset{\sim}{j}$, so it moves parallel to the $y$-axis.
At $t=5$, $\underset{\sim}{v}(5)=2\underset{\sim}{i}$, so it moves parallel to the $x$-axis.
